# SDK 58 (expo@58.0.x) still ships react-native@0.88.0-rc.3, a PRERELEASE.
#
# Per node-semver, a prerelease version satisfies a range only if some
# comparator in that range shares its exact major.minor.patch AND carries a
# prerelease tag. So `0.88.0-rc.3` does not satisfy a plain range like
# `0.86 - 0.88`, even though it falls numerically inside it. npm reports this
# as e.g.
#
#   While resolving: expo58@1.0.0
#   Found: react-native@0.88.0-rc.3
#   Could not resolve dependency:
#   peer react-native@"0.86 - 0.88" from react-native-reanimated@4.7.0
#
# This affects every package declaring a plain `react-native` peer range, so
# it is not fixable by bumping any single dependency. A plain `npm install` of
# the *official* SDK 58 template fails identically.
#
# Keep the SDK-pinned versions and relax peer resolution. Remove this file once
# SDK 58 ships a stable (non-prerelease) react-native, not merely when any one
# package widens its peer range.
legacy-peer-deps=true
